2026-09-27: per-symbol Linux ELF sections; EvoMIR 0.49.

RED: compilation_options::individual_symbol_sections rejected
  -ffunction-sections. Three application-projector tests dropped the positive
  and negative options, and the Kbuild projector did likewise. The latter also
  incorrectly treated a dropped disabling override as unconditionally inert.

Repair: separate, last-option-wins native options, default off. Existing explicit
sections win. Automatic function/data/rodata/PIC-relro/BSS/TLS sections preserve
their flags, type, sizes, alignment, identity and relocations. Aliases share a
target body, constructors/destructors retain registrations, and patch metadata
remains link-ordered. No new IR memory model, retention rule or EqSat transform.
Non-ELF use fails closed; disabled options reproduce baseline assembly exactly.

Subject executable SHA256:
  f21a796f169aa3c0f88b97d6cdccd31210af987f2c9c7b5c9de61bb8e6522c68
driver-symbol-sections.c SHA256:
  4d57620d436a57459c5cf856e8b827e6e78f06351f19ff11d3e3562a31e5e25d

Native matrix in the existing sealed linux/arm64 image:
  GCC14 / Clang19 x O0 / O2 x PIC / static / PIC+CFI+patchable-entry.
  12 unchanged-source reference objects + 12 EvoCC objects, each inspected
  through readelf: section type/flags/alignment, symbol size/TLS type, unique
  placement, explicit overrides and alias identity. Patch records have
  SHF_LINK_ORDER. Both ordinary and --gc-sections links execute: 48/48 PASS.
  Dead external function/data/BSS/readonly/TLS symbols exist before linker GC
  and disappear after GC. Live TLS, callback aliases, constructors/destructors
  and static computed-goto relocations still execute correctly.
  Run: python3 tests/acceptance/symbol-sections-native.py PREPARED_DIRECTORY
  where six sections-evo-O{0,2}-{pic,static,patched}.s files come from the driver.

The first matrix used a nonvolatile constructor-only variable. Clang O2 legally
folded its initialization, so a presence assertion for INIT_ARRAY failed. The
final source uses volatile lifecycle state; this is a test precondition repair,
not a compiler failure or a relaxed assertion. The initial log is retained.

Eight unchanged original musl commands now retain section switches and standard
excess precision. __math_oflow, __math_uflow, frexp and scalbn emit and assemble,
with symbol-named code sections. ceil/floor/rint/rintf still refuse E3021 at the
explicitly excluded scalar-FP asm constraint. Remaining omitted options are
listed in the replay. No original source/expectation changed; no full musl,
libc-test or kernel acceptance is claimed by this small replay.

Focused regressions: 38 CLI option tests, 264 ladder tests, 252 K1 tests PASS;
Ruff PASS. Canonical IR and preprocessing are unchanged by placement options.
Changed-crate gate against 5839dc8: 1051 PASS / zero FAIL / four historical
ignored, 135 result groups; Clippy -D warnings and fmt PASS. No full-workspace
or application result is inferred from the affected-crate count.
Raw logs: .build/floating-targeted/strict-20260927/sections-*.log.
Independent runtime identity remains contracts/build-environment.json's pinned
image/toolchain, not the host assembler.

Reference contract: GCC 14.2 Optimize Options, -ffunction-sections/-fdata-sections
https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-14.2.0/gcc/Optimize-Options.html#index-ffunction-sections
The section flags and runtime claims above are measured, not inferred from docs.
